      <ReportItem port="22" svc_name="ssh" protocol="tcp" severity="1" pluginID="153953" pluginName="SSH Weak Key Exchange Algorithms Enabled" pluginFamily="Misc.">
        <cvss3_base_score>3.7</cvss3_base_score>
        <cvss3_vector>CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N</cvss3_vector>
        <cvss_base_score>2.6</cvss_base_score>
        <cvss_score_rationale>Tenable score for weak key exchange</cvss_score_rationale>
        <cvss_score_source>manual</cvss_score_source>
        <cvss_vector>CVSS2#AV:N/AC:H/Au:N/C:P/I:N/A:N</cvss_vector>
        <description>The remote SSH server is configured to allow key exchange algorithms which are considered weak.

This is based on the IETF draft document Key Exchange (KEX) Method Updates and Recommendations for Secure Shell (SSH) draft-ietf-curdle-ssh-kex-sha2-20. Section 4 lists guidance on key exchange algorithms that SHOULD NOT and MUST NOT be enabled. This includes:

  diffie-hellman-group-exchange-sha1

  diffie-hellman-group1-sha1

  gss-gex-sha1-*

  gss-group1-sha1-*

  gss-group14-sha1-*

  rsa1024-sha1

Note that this plugin only checks for the options of the SSH server, and it does not check for vulnerable software versions.</description>
        <fname>ssh_weak_key_exchange_enabled.nasl</fname>
        <plugin_modification_date>2021/10/13</plugin_modification_date>
